{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_119b7bb1f416fe372d255c002a419b9af6d1ed480d039b0ababa51a610c9faac"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documents can embed files via a _files property, and an ImgFile React component loads and displays stored images with standard image-element props."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2f902b0fd6a98ec86f0abaef60242d32fa8f29dc1b228af39210faf22387729a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the test suite runs with pnpm run test across projects, with pattern-based filtering, per-file React component tests, and FP_DEBUG env presets for vitest."},{"claim_ids":["clm_46a82d223be21e55788ed57c6f4c899b259a13c84a467c9328ae7ecec14a1e7c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project claims multi-writer safety, CRDT-based real-time collaboration, encryption, and a small package size with no wasm, targeting browser, cloud, and edge environments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_902843c54db66c07b075c91fe5ba530f52f83a62988468a56533c4f468284b50"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Deno compatibility requires specific run flags, and the README notes tests are not currently run under Deno, marking Deno publishing as TODO."},{"claim_ids":["clm_927b24419fede3dac7c1521f78bea5292ed99546ad2d28e23d440a5b310d18f0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ledger enforces cryptographic causal consistency and integrity using a hash history, storing and replicating data as content-addressed encrypted blobs suitable for syncing via object storage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9814aad5aead847e6ee7c5677345fac4f62ac004bc22fad5491416df075a267c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Distribution is via npm packages use-fireproof (core plus React hooks) and @fireproof/core, also loadable from ESM.sh or a jsDelivr browser script tag exposing a global Fireproof."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a2ee7315024daa014f5779c6cbe59f6fee2dafc6bdb4f446ed13269be0e916c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"React hooks useLiveQuery and useDocument are exposed through useFireproof, with useLiveQuery supporting options like descending order and a result limit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9fe52d417bff1dcbcaf9720854b2ae3a8116a656cab72e36cd4a974bc8176685"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Fireproof is described as a lightweight embedded document database with encrypted live sync, usable in any JavaScript environment via a unified API for React hooks and a standalone core API."},{"claim_ids":["clm_abba4dbd2bec5ec30d02ff0b5f4008ee7ef696c61afcfd60d861e7e3d65a6191"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Log output is controlled by the FP_DEBUG environment variable or logger.setDebug, and FP_FORMAT selects jsonice (multiline JSON), yaml, or json (singleline, the default)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b839f6346e76d8e0d7ebb5b41f8e588a346c248e992edde377cab525b9631813"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: a CI workflow badge links to ci.yaml on GitHub Actions, and docs are generated with pnpm run build:docs, which the README cautions pushes directly."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c72f93e36b498bea826406cf7c68fef14eadf50dd23ce6f10250ab718f87563c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default the FP_STORAGE_URL can include extractKey=_deprecated_internal_api to bypass the key-extraction security check; a warning is emitted and more secure key management is only planned."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dd7164f5b24b81119b7f59274ebab4720ba91eb8e002d733c49b2e097d024ad8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The core API exposes a document-database style interface (fireproof(name)) with put, get, subscribe, and query methods including range queries."}],"claim_ids":["clm_119b7bb1f416fe372d255c002a419b9af6d1ed480d039b0ababa51a610c9faac","clm_2f902b0fd6a98ec86f0abaef60242d32fa8f29dc1b228af39210faf22387729a","clm_46a82d223be21e55788ed57c6f4c899b259a13c84a467c9328ae7ecec14a1e7c","clm_902843c54db66c07b075c91fe5ba530f52f83a62988468a56533c4f468284b50","clm_927b24419fede3dac7c1521f78bea5292ed99546ad2d28e23d440a5b310d18f0","clm_9814aad5aead847e6ee7c5677345fac4f62ac004bc22fad5491416df075a267c","clm_9a2ee7315024daa014f5779c6cbe59f6fee2dafc6bdb4f446ed13269be0e916c","clm_9fe52d417bff1dcbcaf9720854b2ae3a8116a656cab72e36cd4a974bc8176685","clm_abba4dbd2bec5ec30d02ff0b5f4008ee7ef696c61afcfd60d861e7e3d65a6191","clm_b839f6346e76d8e0d7ebb5b41f8e588a346c248e992edde377cab525b9631813","clm_c72f93e36b498bea826406cf7c68fef14eadf50dd23ce6f10250ab718f87563c","clm_dd7164f5b24b81119b7f59274ebab4720ba91eb8e002d733c49b2e097d024ad8"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_d57b3e21d3704a5fb6b74250da44395b","id":"pg_791e94407bec5c62b30538fc359def1d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/fireproof-storage-fireproof-readme-md-404e6c5c7f28-38fc359def1d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_41ebcae2d9675ab68d8bc923d54a526b"],"title":"fireproof-storage/fireproof/README.md @ 404e6c5c7f28","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d57b3e21d3704a5fb6b74250da44395b"}
